# Every working copy gets LF text files, whatever core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows sets it to true).
# tools/build-preview-5-offline.py hashes the bytes on disk and preview-5-offline-worker.js checks those
# hashes, so a CRLF checkout (new worktree, branch switch, pull) broke the offline manifest and the
# byte-hash checks of the test suites. The repository already stores LF, so this changes no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never convert.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
